# TinyML Experiment Overview

The project contains two application tracks:

1. [IMU motion classification](PARTIE_1_ClassificationVibrations/): acquire six-axis motion data, train a TensorFlow classifier, export TFLite/C-header artifacts and use the Arduino inference sketch.
2. [Electronic-component classification](Partie_2_ClassificationComposants/): capture camera frames, run an exported Edge Impulse classifier and receive results on the host.

See the experiment guides for dependencies, class-label alignment and integration status. The uploaded Node-RED flow provides serial reception; the documented counting dashboard still needs its missing nodes.
